# Gilbert Guide content rules

**Global:** [`preserve-user-edits.mdc`](preserve-user-edits.mdc) — read disk, patch only, never clobber. Applies here too.

## User owns the markdown

- **`content/**/*.md`** — Kate edits by hand (Ctrl+S). Source of truth for project copy.
- **`INDEX.md`** — Kate edits only. **Agents never write, merge, or reformat it** unless she explicitly asks in that message.
- **`npm run build`** — regenerates **`projects-data.js` only**. Must **not** rewrite any `content/**/*.md`.
- **`npm run sync-impact`** / **`projectToMarkdown`** — **rewrites** project markdown. Run **only** when Kate explicitly asks to sync impact / reformat. Prefer patching Impact estimates in place over full file rewrite.

## Do not clobber edits (why Ctrl+S “fails”)

Cursor Save writes the **editor buffer**. If an agent or `sync-impact` then **overwrites the same path on disk**, the tab looks like Save didn’t stick (or shows “file on disk is newer”). **That is clobbering — not a broken Ctrl+S.**

Forbidden unless Kate asked in the same message:

- Bulk find/replace or scripts across `content/projects/*.md` / `retainer.md`
- `npm run sync-impact`, `migrate` / `migrate-to-b2-format`, `format-content`, `apply-campaign-metrics`, or any `projectToMarkdown` write-back
- Copying full **Value icons** from `_TEMPLATE.md` onto a project that already has a trimmed list
- Editing a file she just edited without merging her current wording
- Treating picker package slot **“P6 B1”** as payment plan P6 Event — different things

When she asks to update INDEX → guide: run **`npm run build`** only (reads INDEX into `projects-data.js`). Do **not** rewrite project files unless she asked to change those files.

## Generated vs editable

| File | Who edits |
|------|-----------|
| `content/projects/*.md`, `retainer.md`, `settings.md`, **`INDEX.md`** | Kate |
| `projects-data.js` | build only — do not hand-edit |
